WEBVTT

00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:04.772
Before you start, gather the Allen
key, a hammer, and a spirit level.

00:00:04.772 --> 00:00:09.664
For the half-round table, check the frame
parts, bolts, threaded inserts, pegs,

00:00:09.664 --> 00:00:12.450
cable outlet, and joining
bracket shown here.

00:00:13.740 --> 00:00:14.191
Step 1.

00:00:14.191 --> 00:00:19.149
For the half-round table, lay the frame
pieces upside down on a soft surface.

00:00:19.149 --> 00:00:23.206
Slide the curved rail and straight
rail into the two leg units,

00:00:23.206 --> 00:00:26.490
matching the tabs and holes
shown in the close-ups.

00:00:27.780 --> 00:00:28.697
Steps 2 and 3.

00:00:28.697 --> 00:00:33.411
Tighten four bolts with the Allen key
to secure the first frame section.

00:00:33.411 --> 00:00:36.816
Then slide the next leg unit
onto the straight rail,

00:00:36.816 --> 00:00:41.530
keeping all legs pointing upward
because the frame is still upside down.

00:00:42.820 --> 00:00:43.689
Steps 4 and 5.

00:00:43.689 --> 00:00:47.042
Fit the remaining straight
rail into the open sockets,

00:00:47.042 --> 00:00:50.456
checking that the tabs line
up with the matching holes.

00:00:50.456 --> 00:00:55.485
Tighten five more bolts with the Allen
key so the upside-down frame is square and

00:00:55.485 --> 00:00:55.920
secure.

00:00:57.220 --> 00:00:58.187
Steps 6 and 7.

00:00:58.187 --> 00:01:02.331
Place the half-round tabletop
face down on the soft surface,

00:01:02.331 --> 00:01:05.440
then set the frame on
it and align the holes.

00:01:05.440 --> 00:01:10.620
Screw in five threaded inserts, then
tap five pegs into them with a hammer.

00:01:11.940 --> 00:01:12.394
Step 8.

00:01:12.394 --> 00:01:15.249
Turn the half-round table upright with help.

00:01:15.249 --> 00:01:18.558
Use the adjustable feet to
raise or lower each leg,

00:01:18.558 --> 00:01:22.840
and check the tabletop with a spirit
level until it stands steady.

00:01:24.140 --> 00:01:25.078
Steps 1 and 2.

00:01:25.078 --> 00:01:30.305
For the rectangular table, fasten the
center support between the two long side

00:01:30.305 --> 00:01:32.114
rails with four long bolts.

00:01:32.114 --> 00:01:37.140
Then slide a leg unit onto each rail
end, matching the tabs with the holes.

00:01:38.460 --> 00:01:39.348
Steps 3 and 4.

00:01:39.348 --> 00:01:42.835
Add the remaining rails to
close the rectangular frame,

00:01:42.835 --> 00:01:45.879
making sure every corner
socket is fully seated.

00:01:45.879 --> 00:01:49.810
Tighten eight bolts with the
Allen key at the corner brackets.

00:01:51.100 --> 00:01:52.065
Steps 5 and 6.

00:01:52.065 --> 00:01:57.720
Lay the two tabletop panels face down and
push them together so the center opening

00:01:57.720 --> 00:01:58.340
lines up.

00:01:58.340 --> 00:02:03.650
Place the frame on top, align the holes,
and screw in eight threaded inserts.

00:02:04.940 --> 00:02:05.864
Steps 7 and 8.

00:02:05.864 --> 00:02:10.814
Tap eight pegs into the threaded inserts
to lock the frame to the tabletop.

00:02:10.814 --> 00:02:16.094
With help, turn the table upright and
adjust all four feet until the tabletop is

00:02:16.094 --> 00:02:16.490
level.

00:02:17.780 --> 00:02:18.203
Step 9.

00:02:18.203 --> 00:02:22.308
Press the cable outlet into the
opening in the rectangular tabletop.

00:02:22.308 --> 00:02:25.266
If you are connecting the
half-round table to it,

00:02:25.266 --> 00:02:29.914
place the two joining brackets under
the meeting edge as shown and secure the

00:02:29.914 --> 00:02:30.880
tables together.
